1
00:00:08,960 --> 00:00:13,340
Try lightening up on peace
and stepping away from it

2
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:26,880
aiming for a day floating on the Nakagawa

3
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:33,960
kick a pebble and even your shoes fly off

4
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:42,260
and onto the head of the
carpenter who was saving his money

5
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:48,460
they laughed that I'm still just a kid

6
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:55,580
even if you stir up some energy somewhere,
there's Katsushika Kameari

7
00:00:55,580 --> 00:01:02,500
even a yawn changes nothing,
the streetscape is strangely gentle

8
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:10,460
from the pointy hat's water bottle

9
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:16,780
the sunset falls toward the vast sky

10
00:01:20,940 --> 00:01:25,260
why does tomorrow end too, huh

11
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,400
Katsushika, Shibamata,
even happiness is lost again

12
00:01:39,520 --> 00:01:41,640
I'm the star! Hoshi Tōden!

13
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:45,840
Emergency call! Emergency call!

14
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:48,320
A robbery has occurred at
the Kameari Station-front bank!

15
00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:51,460
The culprit has taken hostages and
barricaded himself inside the bank!

16
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:53,660
Prefectural police officers,
rush to the scene!

17
00:01:54,380 --> 00:01:55,320
Let's go, Nakagawa!

18
00:01:55,940 --> 00:01:56,920
I'll hold the fort!

19
00:01:57,260 --> 00:01:58,100
Understood!

20
00:01:58,420 --> 00:01:59,740
You two, be careful!

21
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:05,240
Wait a second!

22
00:02:06,140 --> 00:02:07,260
What is it, Chief?

23
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:10,140
To solve this case, headquarters

24
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:12,260
is sending over a sharp-witted detective.

25
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:15,140
You two will fall under his command.

26
00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:16,300
What's his name?

27
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:18,100
I don't know much about him either, but

28
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:19,500
his name is something like Hoshi.

29
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:22,420
At headquarters, they apparently
call him the Hardboiled Detective.

30
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:24,020
Hardboiled Detective?

31
00:02:24,020 --> 00:02:26,220
What a cool nickname.

32
00:02:26,220 --> 00:02:30,940
He must be someone straight
out of an old hardboiled movie.

33
00:02:31,460 --> 00:02:32,620
I have a bad feeling about this.

34
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:34,420
Just think about it.

35
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:38,000
Every detective who's shown up in
this pattern before has been useless.

36
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:39,240
Kaipan Deka

37
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:42,020
Moonlight Detective, Venus Detective.

38
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:44,400
There was also Dolphin Detective.

39
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:46,220
Y-yeah, that's true.

40
00:02:46,220 --> 00:02:47,740
So, this time too,

41
00:02:47,740 --> 00:02:51,740
surely some weirdo who'll catch
us off guard is bound to show up.

42
00:02:51,740 --> 00:02:55,260
"Hardboiled" can also mean
"half-boiled, Tanbar 5," you know.

43
00:02:55,260 --> 00:02:55,740
That's it.

44
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:58,420
So maybe he eats boiled eggs
all the time or something.

45
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:02,420
Maybe he has smooth skin like a boiled egg.

46
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:05,880
Or maybe he's wearing a giant eggshell.

47
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:08,160
Either way, he's no ordinary man.

48
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:10,820
Yeah, you'd better brace
yourselves thoroughly.

49
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:14,400
Ridiculous, there's no way some weird
detective would show up so easily.

50
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:18,260
You're naive, Chief. Have you
forgotten our bitter experiences so far?

51
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:23,560
It's a Camaro, I'd say.

52
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:24,900
Could he be among these people?

53
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:29,420
He's the star sent from headquarters.

54
00:03:29,860 --> 00:03:33,180
People call me the Hardboiled Dega.

55
00:03:33,180 --> 00:03:35,160
He's surprisingly normal.

56
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:36,640
No, we can't let our guard down.

57
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:39,440
Here it comes... the hard-boiled egg!

58
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:44,340
What, it's just cigarettes?

59
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:46,020
No, I don't think that's all there is.

60
00:03:46,020 --> 00:03:47,780
He must still be hiding something.

61
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:50,260
This time, it's really coming out!

62
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,960
What, it's just a lighter?

63
00:03:56,220 --> 00:03:58,600
Weren't you just wanting a cigarette?

64
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,500
Ryo-san, you're overthinking it.

65
00:04:04,060 --> 00:04:05,880
Right then, men, let's head to the scene!

66
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:07,900
Looks like it's going
to be hardboiled, then.

67
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:10,940
Aren't you going to serve up the boiled egg?

68
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:14,720
Hey! Making me pull a
silly gag face like that!

69
00:04:14,720 --> 00:04:16,080
What do you mean, boiled egg!

70
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:18,120
I'm a hardboiled detective, you know!

71
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:20,300
Why on earth should I have
to serve something like that?

72
00:04:20,300 --> 00:04:21,880
Well, when you ask why...

73
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:23,680
I just felt something was lacking.

74
00:04:24,140 --> 00:04:25,640
What are you lot babbling about!

75
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:28,520
Arriving right away in a Camaro,

76
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:30,440
suddenly, with a frightening Happy Strike,

77
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:31,920
lighting up with a Gauloises lighter,

78
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:33,980
and now, this cool signature line.

79
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:36,240
I'm too cool, way too cool!

80
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:38,340
I'm so stylish, I'm intoxicated by myself.

81
00:04:38,340 --> 00:04:40,980
With this, the hardboiled atmosphere

82
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:43,880
isn't floating around at all!

83
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:45,380
What is this show?

84
00:04:45,380 --> 00:04:47,960
This is just like an everyday comedy anime!

85
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:50,520
With this, my hardboiled charm

86
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:51,880
can't be fully displayed.

87
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:53,520
What is this guy talking about?

88
00:04:57,200 --> 00:04:59,680
This background is no good, change it.

89
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:09,760
Good, this is the perfect
backdrop for a hardboiled man.

90
00:05:09,760 --> 00:05:14,280
Next, you characters need
to get more realistic too.

91
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:18,860
I'm getting realistic here.

92
00:05:19,700 --> 00:05:20,620
Something like this...

93
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:21,680
No way.

94
00:05:23,640 --> 00:05:25,480
This is like something
out of a gekiga comic!

95
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:28,060
Some crazy guy has shown up!

96
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:34,020
This is truly fitting for a hardboiled man.

97
00:05:34,020 --> 00:05:35,880
It's a hardboiled world.

98
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:40,360
Now I'll redo my entrance scene.

99
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:46,580
Hey, we don't have time to be so leisurely!

100
00:05:46,580 --> 00:05:47,140
Lord Ryo

101
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:50,420
The clock has gone back three minutes.

102
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:54,120
Doesn't that mean we have to
start over before we can move on?

103
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:58,560
So that's it. It can't be helped. Much as it galls me,
we have no choice but to do what he says.

104
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:00,900
What were we talking
about three minutes ago?

105
00:06:01,380 --> 00:06:06,000
I think it was around when I said he's no ordinary man,
either way.

106
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:09,940
Right, then let's start from there. Everyone,
get back to the positions you were in at that time!

107
00:06:09,940 --> 00:06:12,360
Do I have to do this too?

108
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:16,900
Of course, Chief. If you're not here,
the conversation won't work at all.

109
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:18,200
Are you all ready?

110
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:19,560
Okay.

111
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:24,893
All right, then,
Hardboiled Detective entrance scene, Take 2,

112
00:06:24,943 --> 00:06:26,120
Ready, action!

113
00:06:29,500 --> 00:06:31,680
Either way, he's no ordinary man, is he?

114
00:06:32,020 --> 00:06:34,380
Yeah, you'd better be well prepared.

115
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:41,780
How ridiculous. There's no way some
weird detective would show up that quickly.

116
00:06:42,100 --> 00:06:45,760
You're naive, Chief. Have you
forgotten our bitter experiences so far?

117
00:06:55,020 --> 00:06:55,840
It's a Camaro.

118
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:57,520
Could it be that, in there,

119
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:08,900
I'm the star from headquarters.

120
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:12,760
People call me the Hardboiled Detective.

121
00:07:17,940 --> 00:07:19,300
Satisfied now?

122
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:21,880
Hold on a second.

123
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:25,100
What do you mean? We redid it in hardboiled style for you,
didn't we?

124
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:29,040
No, I still feel like it's
lacking that hardboiled edge.

125
00:07:30,260 --> 00:07:33,860
Right, let's make the screen sepia-toned and go for a cool,
rugged look.

126
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:37,440
It looks like a 1940s Hollywood movie.

127
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:39,320
Somehow it does look cool, doesn't it.

128
00:07:39,320 --> 00:07:42,540
Not the departure,
but a set change in 1940s style!

129
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:49,000
Why do I have to

130
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:56,340
Alright,
now we're doing the current scene again

131
00:07:56,340 --> 00:07:57,600
Are we really doing this again?

132
00:07:57,600 --> 00:08:01,040
Alright,
Hardboiled Detective entrance scene, Take 3

133
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:02,880
Ready, action!

134
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:11,400
Either way, he's no ordinary man, is he?

135
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:14,360
Yeah, we'd better be fully prepared for it.

136
00:08:17,960 --> 00:08:18,860
How ridiculous.

137
00:08:18,860 --> 00:08:20,960
No way some weird detective
would show up that easily.

138
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:22,720
You're naive, Chief.

139
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:25,300
Have you forgotten our
bitter experiences so far?

140
00:08:33,600 --> 00:08:34,600
It's a Camaro.

141
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:36,360
Could it be that inside there's

142
00:08:39,180 --> 00:08:40,860
the star from headquarters?

143
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:44,980
People call me the Hardboiled Detective.

144
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:46,540
No good.

145
00:08:46,540 --> 00:08:49,800
Like this, we can't even tell
what color the red Camaro is.

146
00:08:50,420 --> 00:08:51,760
You should've noticed that earlier.

147
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:53,760
Let's go with color after all.

148
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:56,760
Back to normal.

149
00:08:57,440 --> 00:09:00,600
How do we make this look as
sharp as a hardboiled movie?

150
00:09:00,600 --> 00:09:02,460
Just give up already.

151
00:09:02,460 --> 00:09:06,900
Aren't TV and movie screens
different sizes to begin with?

152
00:09:06,900 --> 00:09:08,940
The screen size, that's it!

153
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:10,300
Unnecessary remarks.

154
00:09:10,860 --> 00:09:11,440
Sorry.

155
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:13,700
Right, let's change the screen size.

156
00:09:13,700 --> 00:09:14,900
CinemaScope size.

157
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:20,660
Don't you lot be lounging
around outside the frame!

158
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:22,180
S-sorry.

159
00:09:22,180 --> 00:09:23,480
S-sorry, Ryo-sama.

160
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:25,080
What a hopeless bunch.

161
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:26,300
Get it right, will you!

162
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:29,160
Now then, the hardboiled entrance, Take 4.

163
00:09:29,160 --> 00:09:31,000
Ready, action!

164
00:09:33,760 --> 00:09:36,040
Either way, he's no ordinary man, is he.

165
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:38,620
Yeah, we'd better brace ourselves.

166
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:44,620
How ridiculous. As if some weird
detective would really show up.

167
00:09:44,620 --> 00:09:49,580
Hey, Hondana, why are you here?
This is the Chief's line, damn it!

168
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:52,420
It's not like I want
to be doing this either!

169
00:09:52,420 --> 00:09:55,740
I only came to see my senior,
and suddenly Chief Ohara

170
00:09:55,740 --> 00:09:58,260
handed me this script and said,
"Leave the rest to you."

171
00:09:58,260 --> 00:10:01,580
Hey, that's not fair!
The Chief ran off alone!

172
00:10:01,580 --> 00:10:02,620
Seriously, wait!

173
00:10:02,620 --> 00:10:06,340
Hey! Don't change the cast on your own!

174
00:10:06,340 --> 00:10:08,820
Don't blame us,
the Chief is the one who ran away!

175
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:11,360
Did Chief Ohara say anything else?

176
00:10:11,580 --> 00:10:14,600
I can't keep up with this anymore.
I'm exhausted.

177
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:17,200
We don't want to keep
going along with this either!

178
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:21,060
Since the Chief's already gone,
let's just call this scene off.

179
00:10:21,060 --> 00:10:24,660
Idiot! This is the lead's entrance scene!

180
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:25,980
We can't just cancel it!

181
00:10:26,340 --> 00:10:28,220
But the Chief isn't here...

182
00:10:28,860 --> 00:10:32,180
There's no choice.
You'll have to play the Chief's part.

183
00:10:32,180 --> 00:10:33,040
Makeup!

184
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:40,000
Let's change the camera angle.

185
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,080
We'll make sure not to show his face.

186
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:47,780
That's good.

187
00:10:47,780 --> 00:10:50,780
Then, hardboiled detective
entrance scene, Take 5.

188
00:10:50,780 --> 00:10:52,220
Ready, action!

189
00:10:54,780 --> 00:10:56,900
Either way, he's no ordinary man, is he.

190
00:10:56,900 --> 00:10:59,420
Yeah, you'd better be prepared for anything.

191
00:11:00,420 --> 00:11:03,560
Yeah, ridiculous. There's no way a
weird detective would really show up.

192
00:11:04,020 --> 00:11:07,440
You're naive, Chief. Have you
forgotten our bitter experiences so far?

193
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:11,600
It's the Camaro.

194
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:13,620
What if he's inside...

195
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:17,760
I'm Hoshi, from headquarters.

196
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:22,120
People call me the Hardboiled Detective.

197
00:11:24,340 --> 00:11:25,600
Finally, a good take.

198
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:29,900
The camera was pointing
down the whole time, senpai.

199
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:31,760
Hoshi-san's face isn't
even in the shot, is it?

200
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:35,060
Actually, it seemed like only
everyone's legs were in the shot.

201
00:11:35,060 --> 00:11:38,380
Right, with that,
you can't tell what's going on at all.

202
00:11:38,380 --> 00:11:41,640
If he hears us,
we'll have to reshoot it again!

203
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:43,760
We can't push it any further,
this is getting ridiculous.

204
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:47,000
Alright, this scene's a wrap.
Next one, let's go!

205
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:49,660
Luckily, Hoshi-san is absorbed
in his own performance,

206
00:11:49,660 --> 00:11:52,040
so he doesn't seem to
have noticed any of this.

207
00:11:52,860 --> 00:11:56,860
That was a splendid entrance,
truly worthy of a hardboiled style.

208
00:11:58,700 --> 00:12:01,600
So that means we're still
stuck at the police box

209
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:05,740
Hoshi's entrance alone used up the entire first half,
you know.

210
00:12:05,740 --> 00:12:08,100
Because of that,
the story hasn't moved forward at all!

211
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:10,300
We're picking up the
pace in the second half!

212
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:12,880
But it has to stay hardboiled, mind you.

213
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:15,320
Fine, fine,
just hurry up and move the story along.

214
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:15,660
Good.

215
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:17,360
What is it?

216
00:12:17,960 --> 00:12:20,980
Can I just step back now, then?

217
00:12:23,460 --> 00:12:26,000
Looks like Chief Ohara has no more lines

218
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,020
You're dismissed.

219
00:12:27,940 --> 00:12:29,940
Alright, then I'll be heading out first.

220
00:12:30,460 --> 00:12:31,220
Good work, everyone.

221
00:12:32,480 --> 00:12:35,040
So, who's going to be under me?

222
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:36,620
Has this already started?

223
00:12:36,620 --> 00:12:37,380
Looks like it.

224
00:12:37,380 --> 00:12:40,460
I'm asking who's joining my unit.

225
00:12:40,460 --> 00:12:42,080
I heard it's two people.

226
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:44,060
Yes, that's us.

227
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:46,120
Officer Keiichi Nakagawa.

228
00:12:46,520 --> 00:12:48,460
Sergeant Kankichi Ryotsu, sir.

229
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:51,680
Alright, get in my car, Ryotsu, Nakagawa.

230
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:53,600
We're heading straight for Kameari Station.

231
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:55,180
Perfect.

232
00:12:55,820 --> 00:12:57,940
That came out perfectly
in one take this time.

233
00:12:57,940 --> 00:12:59,500
Even I'm impressed with myself.

234
00:12:59,500 --> 00:13:01,960
Now straight into the next scene,
full speed.

235
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:05,880
Go!

236
00:13:16,260 --> 00:13:16,900
Wait a minute.

237
00:13:20,160 --> 00:13:21,380
Don't stop so suddenly.

238
00:13:22,040 --> 00:13:23,800
No good! That take is no good!

239
00:13:23,900 --> 00:13:26,140
There was nothing wrong with it!

240
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:28,680
The dispatch scene is supposed
to be the biggest highlight.

241
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:31,840
It's the spot where it has
to look the most hardboiled.

242
00:13:32,100 --> 00:13:33,840
But something was missing.

243
00:13:34,060 --> 00:13:35,400
You're really going to redo it again?!

244
00:13:35,860 --> 00:13:36,980
What exactly was missing?

245
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:38,860
That's it! Backlighting!

246
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:40,380
Backlighting?

247
00:13:40,740 --> 00:13:42,220
What's backlighting?

248
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:46,240
You'll see. Add backlighting to
that scene and we'll do it again.

249
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:48,900
Hardboiled dispatch scene, Take 2!

250
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:50,680
Ready, and action!

251
00:13:53,220 --> 00:13:53,880
Go!

252
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:58,420
Why is it nighttime?

253
00:13:58,420 --> 00:13:59,300
Dunno.

254
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:04,260
Wow, so this is the Tokoh Kakoh?
It's cool, isn't it?

255
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:06,900
But why did it suddenly turn to night?

256
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:11,060
To make the Tokoh Kakoh shine beautifully,
the background has to be night.

257
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:15,480
A robbery just happened at the bank in front of the station!
At night, it won't add up!

258
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:18,880
Shut up. Once we get there,
we can just switch it back to day, can't we?

259
00:14:19,520 --> 00:14:21,360
What a convenient excuse...

260
00:14:22,040 --> 00:14:24,900
Excuse me,
where exactly are we driving right now?

261
00:14:25,220 --> 00:14:26,620
On the Metropolitan Expressway at night.

262
00:14:27,020 --> 00:14:30,580
We're headed for Kameari Station,
so why are we on the expressway?

263
00:14:30,780 --> 00:14:31,851
Ugh, you're so annoying.

264
00:14:31,901 --> 00:14:35,040
In hardboiled movies, cars always
drive on the expressway at night.

265
00:14:35,260 --> 00:14:36,400
What nonsense.

266
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,620
Visuals come before logic.

267
00:14:40,020 --> 00:14:40,840
Wait a minute!

268
00:14:42,740 --> 00:14:44,040
What now?

269
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:46,340
No good. Something's still missing.

270
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:49,240
I think it was hardboiled
enough already, though.

271
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:50,680
What exactly do you think is missing?

272
00:14:52,040 --> 00:14:52,680
Music?

273
00:14:52,980 --> 00:14:56,700
At times like this, the show's theme song
should be playing in the background, right?

274
00:14:56,700 --> 00:14:57,840
Now that you mention it,

275
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:59,260
that's true, I suppose.

276
00:14:59,260 --> 00:15:02,040
Put the theme song into
this scene and do it again!

277
00:15:02,040 --> 00:15:03,340
Are we really doing this?

278
00:15:03,560 --> 00:15:04,300
Of course.

279
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:06,320
Hardboiled, for the dispatch scene?

280
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:07,120
Take 3.

281
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:08,900
Ready, action!

282
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:11,940
Launch!

283
00:15:13,780 --> 00:15:16,880
Didn't you say the second
half would pick up the tempo?

284
00:15:17,160 --> 00:15:19,240
Yet this is already the third time.

285
00:15:33,900 --> 00:15:36,220
So this was the theme song.

286
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:38,640
That's what I told you, damn it.

287
00:15:38,640 --> 00:15:40,600
No, there must be other songs too.

288
00:15:41,820 --> 00:15:43,080
Music Star.

289
00:15:44,120 --> 00:15:44,560
No.

290
00:15:50,260 --> 00:15:51,400
This one's wrong too.

291
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:55,280
Summer has come again this year.

292
00:15:55,280 --> 00:15:58,620
Summer's over! Forget it! No music here!

293
00:15:58,840 --> 00:16:02,880
Let's always keep smiling.

294
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:04,880
I told you no music is fine, damn it!

295
00:16:23,020 --> 00:16:25,920
Hey, it really is noon already.
What on earth is going on?

296
00:16:26,340 --> 00:16:29,320
I've stopped being surprised
by anything that happens.

297
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:32,320
The culprit hasn't made any demands yet.

298
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:33,120
I see.

299
00:16:34,700 --> 00:16:36,600
This day is getting way too long.

300
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,660
Nakagawa.

301
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:41,700
Hey, stop squealing over there!

302
00:16:41,700 --> 00:16:45,360
You're ruining the hardboiled scene!

303
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:48,820
But Nakagawa is so cool!

304
00:16:48,820 --> 00:16:49,660
Well, it can't be helped.

305
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:50,880
So cool.

306
00:16:53,760 --> 00:17:00,240
How could a weakling like this be cool?
Not at all, not one bit, not even a little!

307
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:04,340
This is why people who can't understand
hardboiled are such a nuisance.

308
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:08,640
Truly cool means a rugged man like me.

309
00:17:09,300 --> 00:17:13,320
Not at all, not one bit,
not even a little, is he rugged.

310
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:18,620
Fine, I'll make it simple enough even
for fangirls like you to understand.

311
00:17:20,340 --> 00:17:23,780
Somehow Hoshi's face suddenly
looks more chiseled, like...

312
00:17:24,280 --> 00:17:25,640
What's going on here?

313
00:17:26,380 --> 00:17:27,720
Just take a good look.

314
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:29,480
Zoom in.

315
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:36,360
What is this?

316
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:38,280
Isn't this mitochondria?

317
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:40,400
Oops, we went too close-up.

318
00:17:40,780 --> 00:17:41,800
Let's pull back a little.

319
00:17:45,980 --> 00:17:47,960
Look closely at the area around the eyes.

320
00:17:48,620 --> 00:17:51,320
What happened here?
The shadow's in three tiers.

321
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:59,560
You noticed By making the shadow three tiers,
we create deeper shading,

322
00:17:59,560 --> 00:18:03,000
which lets us give him
a hardboiled expression.

323
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:08,660
Our shadows are only one tier,
and then it goes to four, five, six tiers!

324
00:18:08,660 --> 00:18:12,600
See? This is what hardboiled
coolness is all about.

325
00:18:13,140 --> 00:18:14,840
It's creepy.

326
00:18:14,840 --> 00:18:16,240
It's too realistic, it's eerie.

327
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:20,060
Even with only one tier of shadow,
Nakagawa is way better.

328
00:18:22,180 --> 00:18:25,900
You lot don't understand hardboiled, so you
don't even deserve a single layer of shadow.

329
00:18:26,520 --> 00:18:28,760
Better become a shadowless,
two-head-tall chibi character.

330
00:18:28,760 --> 00:18:35,340
Shut up.

331
00:18:35,900 --> 00:18:37,320
I have no more use for you all.

332
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:38,320
With frame art.

333
00:18:40,340 --> 00:18:41,500
The nuisances are gone.

334
00:18:41,500 --> 00:18:44,240
Now we can keep the hardboiled world intact.

335
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:48,500
I can't take it anymore, acting however you
please just because you're a guest character!

336
00:18:48,500 --> 00:18:51,600
In that case,
I'll show you the power of the lead, me!

337
00:18:53,160 --> 00:18:56,920
How should I resolve this
situation in a hardboiled way?

338
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:59,040
Here come the footsteps of a gag manga.

339
00:19:02,260 --> 00:19:04,440
Did I just hear some weird sound?

340
00:19:04,940 --> 00:19:08,840
Maybe it's my imagination, but I
guess we have no choice but to storm in.

341
00:19:09,920 --> 00:19:11,680
Footsteps of a robot anime.

342
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:17,040
It sounded like another weird noise again.

343
00:19:17,040 --> 00:19:18,320
Must be my imagination.

344
00:19:26,220 --> 00:19:29,940
This is the biggest showcase for hardboiled,
isn't it?

345
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:34,700
Then the old lady's laughter

346
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:36,640
W-what?

347
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:40,780
It's not like my fly is open or anything.

348
00:19:41,160 --> 00:19:43,320
Or my clothes are torn somewhere.

349
00:19:44,840 --> 00:19:53,160
It must have been my imagination. A man who lives in the hardboiled world like me should have nothing to do with an old lady's laughter.
There it is again, the old lady's laugh!

350
00:19:55,740 --> 00:19:58,500
What was that laugh? Back off!

351
00:19:58,840 --> 00:20:06,460
Don't go adding laughter on your own!
Shut up! You're the one who's been doing whatever you want until now! I'm the star of this show!

352
00:20:06,460 --> 00:20:08,840
What's wrong with doing what I want?

353
00:20:10,260 --> 00:20:11,420
What's so funny?

354
00:20:11,420 --> 00:20:12,880
You, the star?

355
00:20:13,780 --> 00:20:16,640
You're not the true star of this show.

356
00:20:17,340 --> 00:20:18,560
Just watch.

357
00:20:28,320 --> 00:20:30,260
Isn't this the show's opening?

358
00:20:30,260 --> 00:20:31,120
So what?

359
00:20:31,120 --> 00:20:33,420
Read this title for a moment.

360
00:20:33,420 --> 00:20:35,580
No need to tell me, I already know.

361
00:20:36,460 --> 00:20:38,380
Katsushika-ku Kameari Kōen-mae Hashutsujo

362
00:20:38,380 --> 00:20:40,020
Abbreviated, it's "Kochikame," isn't it?

363
00:20:40,020 --> 00:20:43,500
Yes, that's Katsushika-ku
Kameari Kōen-mae Hashutsujo.

364
00:20:43,500 --> 00:20:45,360
This is the title of this show.

365
00:20:45,360 --> 00:20:47,900
There's no word like "Ryotsu" anywhere.

366
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:49,820
Sorry.

367
00:20:49,820 --> 00:20:52,320
The protagonist of this
show is the police box,

368
00:20:52,320 --> 00:20:54,260
and you're merely a supporting character.

369
00:20:58,100 --> 00:20:59,360
So that's how it was.

370
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:01,800
So I wasn't the lead?

371
00:21:02,620 --> 00:21:06,160
It took you over two years since the
broadcast started to finally notice?

372
00:21:08,080 --> 00:21:08,820
Hold on!

373
00:21:08,920 --> 00:21:12,180
Even if Hashutsujo is the protagonist,
it's a building, so it can't move!

374
00:21:12,580 --> 00:21:15,220
That's what animation is for.
We'll give it hands and feet.

375
00:21:15,540 --> 00:21:18,760
This is Kameari Kōen-mae Hashutsujo.
We're making it Hashutsujo-kun.

376
00:21:18,880 --> 00:21:21,560
I'm Hashutsujo-kun. Nice to meet you!

377
00:21:22,540 --> 00:21:23,860
Hashutsujo-kun runs!

378
00:21:24,060 --> 00:21:25,080
Yah, hi!

379
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:26,580
Hashutsujo-kun trips!

380
00:21:27,040 --> 00:21:28,480
I fell down!

381
00:21:28,660 --> 00:21:29,960
Hashutsujo-kun does a handstand!

382
00:21:30,400 --> 00:21:31,460
Yoisho!

383
00:21:31,700 --> 00:21:33,100
Hashutsujo-kun eats ramen!

384
00:21:33,920 --> 00:21:35,840
Hashutsujo-kun watches TV!

385
00:21:38,340 --> 00:21:40,980
You just happened to be
posted at the police box,

386
00:21:40,980 --> 00:21:43,020
so you get to wear a lead's face.

387
00:21:43,580 --> 00:21:45,580
If I were the one posted at the police box,

388
00:21:45,580 --> 00:21:48,300
it would be a story
where I shine as the hero.

389
00:21:48,300 --> 00:21:50,360
How dare you!
Are you trying to take over my role?

390
00:21:51,100 --> 00:21:53,720
Men as hardboiled as I am

391
00:21:53,720 --> 00:21:55,800
are simply more fitting for the regular role,
that's all.

392
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:59,240
Someone like you could never handle a regular role!
Absolutely not!

393
00:22:06,020 --> 00:22:06,660
Wait.

394
00:22:07,580 --> 00:22:09,280
I prefer Ryu, personally.

395
00:22:09,280 --> 00:22:10,440
Swap him out for me.

396
00:22:10,440 --> 00:22:14,880
Don't say something so lame
during the signature pose.

397
00:22:15,440 --> 00:22:18,520
That's the attention to detail
a hardboiled man demands.

398
00:22:18,520 --> 00:22:21,980
Fine, let's settle it once and for all:
which of us deserves to be the show's regular.

399
00:22:21,980 --> 00:22:22,860
Very well.

400
00:22:25,840 --> 00:22:29,660
Then whoever arrests the
criminal holed up over there wins.

401
00:22:29,660 --> 00:22:30,700
You're on.

402
00:22:30,700 --> 00:22:31,960
Then the contest begins!

403
00:22:37,740 --> 00:22:39,100
We've arrested the criminal.

404
00:22:42,900 --> 00:22:45,040
Suddenly it's evening!

405
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:47,040
What's the meaning of this,
Director Takamatsu?

406
00:22:48,400 --> 00:22:50,720
We've run considerably
over the broadcast time,

407
00:22:50,720 --> 00:22:53,280
so we cut all the arrest scenes.

408
00:22:53,280 --> 00:22:54,180
What?

409
00:22:54,780 --> 00:22:56,640
Hey, then what about the contest?

410
00:22:56,640 --> 00:22:58,660
We'll have to settle it another time.

411
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:00,320
No way.

412
00:23:02,020 --> 00:23:03,320
This is outrageous.

413
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:05,040
My big moment...

414
00:23:07,480 --> 00:23:08,880
What? The background's disappeared!

415
00:23:09,340 --> 00:23:13,620
That's because you keep making such unreasonable
demands that the background artist ran off!

416
00:23:13,620 --> 00:23:14,120
What?

417
00:23:15,600 --> 00:23:16,840
Hey, the colors are gone too!

418
00:23:16,840 --> 00:23:18,880
Looks like the colorist ran off too.

419
00:23:18,880 --> 00:23:21,480
What do you mean?
Isn't the movement weird too?

420
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:23,280
It's talking,
but its mouth isn't even moving!

421
00:23:23,820 --> 00:23:25,500
Looks like the inbetweeners ran off too

422
00:23:26,260 --> 00:23:27,960
What's this number? It's way too big!

423
00:23:28,320 --> 00:23:30,340
That's called a cel number, you know.

424
00:23:30,860 --> 00:23:31,960
And these speech bubbles too,

425
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:34,120
just talk along with them.

426
00:23:35,040 --> 00:23:38,100
It's becoming like a dubbing session
where the film isn't ready in time.

427
00:23:38,780 --> 00:23:40,120
W-what are these lines?

428
00:23:40,120 --> 00:23:42,020
Even Genga-man has finally run off.

429
00:23:42,020 --> 00:23:45,360
Hey, with this, nobody can tell what's what!

430
00:23:47,680 --> 00:23:49,860
So what happened to Hoshi-san?

431
00:23:50,420 --> 00:23:53,300
No idea. All the drawings have disappeared,
after all.

432
00:23:53,300 --> 00:23:55,340
We don't even know which way he went.

433
00:23:55,340 --> 00:23:57,920
This episode was a total mess, wasn't it?

434
00:23:57,920 --> 00:23:59,820
I don't want him showing up again, not ever!

435
00:24:04,380 --> 00:24:06,680
Now, next week's Day 5 is

436
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:11,800
Hey, what's this?
You just pop out on your own, you idiot!

437
00:24:11,800 --> 00:24:16,440
No way, Tsukushō!
I'll definitely appear again, just you wait!

438
00:24:16,840 --> 00:24:19,020
Because of you, I couldn't read
the scrolling captions, you know!

439
00:24:19,520 --> 00:24:22,100
Next time, Bodyguard of Love, got it?

440
00:24:35,720 --> 00:24:43,860
Shock and uproar, with spirit,
with resolution, swiftly, with settlement

441
00:24:43,860 --> 00:24:55,680
decided, with inspiration, bouncing,
summed up, in action, flying away

442
00:24:56,760 --> 00:25:00,300
Above all, amazing power!

443
00:25:00,620 --> 00:25:06,400
Everyone gather, come here!

444
00:25:07,080 --> 00:25:12,680
Like a dream, the final energy

445
00:25:13,700 --> 00:25:17,120
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday

446
00:25:17,120 --> 00:25:20,000
Drawing the universe, standing on the ground

447
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:23,800
Kameari's star spun
around and traced a circle

448
00:25:26,180 --> 00:25:27,440
This should be good enough, right?

449
00:25:27,440 --> 00:25:28,940
Like hell it is!

